## Part 4 — Backfill script

Create `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/scripts/backfill-webp.php`.

The `scripts/` directory does not currently exist; it must be created first (`mkdir scripts`).

```php
<?php
/**
 * scripts/backfill-webp.php
 *
 * CLI-only. Iterates every jpg/jpeg/png/gif under uploads/ and ensures
 * a .webp sibling exists, using the same ImageProcessor logic as imageUpload().
 *
 * Usage:
 *   php scripts/backfill-webp.php [--dry-run]
 *
 * Options:
 *   --dry-run   Print what would be processed, do not create files.
 */

// Guard: CLI only
if (PHP_SAPI !== 'cli') {
    http_response_code(403);
    exit('CLI only.' . PHP_EOL);
}

$isDryRun = in_array('--dry-run', $argv ?? [], true);

// Bootstrap: resolve project root the same way base.class.php does
$dir = __DIR__;
$projectRoot = null;
while ($dir !== dirname($dir)) {
    if (is_file($dir . '/src/autoload.php')) {
        $projectRoot = $dir;
        break;
    }
    $dir = dirname($dir);
}

if ($projectRoot === null) {
    fwrite(STDERR, '[backfill-webp] ERROR: Could not find project root (missing src/autoload.php).' . PHP_EOL);
    exit(1);
}

require_once $projectRoot . '/src/autoload.php';

use Core\ImageProcessor;

$uploadsDir = $projectRoot . '/uploads';

if (!is_dir($uploadsDir)) {
    fwrite(STDERR, '[backfill-webp] ERROR: uploads/ directory not found at: ' . $uploadsDir . PHP_EOL);
    exit(1);
}

$convertible = ['jpg', 'jpeg', 'png', 'gif'];

// Recursive iterator over uploads/
$iterator = new RecursiveIteratorIterator(
    new RecursiveDirectoryIterator($uploadsDir, FilesystemIterator::SKIP_DOTS)
);

$countCreated = 0;
$countSkipped = 0;
$countFailed  = 0;
$countTotal   = 0;

foreach ($iterator as $fileInfo) {
    /** @var SplFileInfo $fileInfo */
    if (!$fileInfo->isFile()) {
        continue;
    }

    $ext = strtolower($fileInfo->getExtension());
    if (!in_array($ext, $convertible, true)) {
        continue;
    }

    $absolutePath = str_replace('\\', '/', $fileInfo->getRealPath());
    $webpPath     = (string) preg_replace('/\.[^.]+$/', '.webp', $absolutePath);
    $countTotal++;

    if (is_file($webpPath)) {
        echo '[skip]    ' . $absolutePath . PHP_EOL;
        $countSkipped++;
        continue;
    }

    if ($isDryRun) {
        echo '[dry-run] would create: ' . $webpPath . PHP_EOL;
        $countCreated++;
        continue;
    }

    $result = ImageProcessor::makeWebpSibling($absolutePath);

    if ($result) {
        echo '[created] ' . $webpPath . PHP_EOL;
        $countCreated++;
    } else {
        fwrite(STDERR, '[FAILED]  ' . $absolutePath . PHP_EOL);
        $countFailed++;
    }
}

echo PHP_EOL;
echo '--- Summary ---' . PHP_EOL;
echo 'Convertible files found : ' . $countTotal    . PHP_EOL;
echo 'WebP created            : ' . $countCreated  . PHP_EOL;
echo 'Already had WebP        : ' . $countSkipped  . PHP_EOL;
echo 'Failed                  : ' . $countFailed   . PHP_EOL;

exit($countFailed > 0 ? 1 : 0);
```

**Key design decisions in the script:**

- Uses the same `no_find_project_root()` walk strategy as `base.class.php` but re-implements it inline (to avoid importing the full bootstrap stack in CLI context, which would try to start sessions and load DB credentials).
- Requires only `src/autoload.php` to get the `Core\ImageProcessor` class — no DB, no session, no HTTP objects needed.
- `is_file($webpPath)` check before calling `makeWebpSibling` avoids unnecessary Spatie/Image processing for files that already have a sibling (idempotent, safe to re-run).
- `--dry-run` flag allows safe auditing before committing to disk writes.
- Exit code `1` when any file failed, `0` on clean run — suitable for CI or cron.
- Existing uploads at `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/uploads/` currently have no `.webp` files at all (confirmed by search above), so the first run will process all 6+ found files.

